{
  "name": "The specimen and the seal",
  "summary": "TshepoVet's world is official paper: CIPC certificates, SARS PIN letters, B-BBEE affidavits, the supplier's passport. Security printing gives the vocabulary, used sparingly: the guilloche seal is the only ornament, stamps carry verdicts, the sandbox is marked as a specimen, and everything else is quiet: cool security paper, petrol ink, records with their 'as of' dates.",
  "rules": [
    "Every text pair is 7:1 or better (WCAG 1.4.6, AAA); control edges are 3:1 or better.",
    "Violet, green and red are never decoration: violet is 'you can do this', the stamp colours are verdicts.",
    "Radii by hierarchy: a stamp is sharp, a control softer, a record sheet the softest.",
    "Body text 16px with a 1.6 line height, under 72 characters a line; never justified.",
    "Every target at least 44 by 44 pixels; a 3px focus ring with an offset; a skip link first.",
    "No sideways scrolling at 320 pixels; reduced motion respected; no time limits."
  ],
